## Building a Calculator

### Calculator State

```xiom
type Calculator {
  current_value: Int;
  memory: Int;
  history: Vec[Str];
  last_result: Int;
}

fn create_calculator() -> Calculator {
  Calculator{ current_value: 0, memory: 0, history: Vec[Str].new(), last_result: 0 }
}
```

### Operations

```xiom
enum Operation {
  Add; Subtract; Multiply; Divide;
  Store; Recall; Clear;
  ShowHistory;
}

fn execute(calc: &mut Calculator, op: Operation, operand: Int) -> Int {
  match op {
    Operation.Add => { calc.last_result = calc.current_value + operand; },
    Operation.Subtract => { calc.last_result = calc.current_value - operand; },
    Operation.Multiply => { calc.last_result = calc.current_value * operand; },
    Operation.Divide => {
      if operand == 0 { return -1; };
      calc.last_result = calc.current_value / operand;
    },
    Operation.Store => { calc.memory = calc.current_value; },
    Operation.Recall => { calc.current_value = calc.memory; },
    Operation.Clear => { calc.current_value = 0; },
    Operation.ShowHistory => { },
  };

  let entry = format_entry(op, operand, calc.last_result);
  calc.history.push(entry);
  calc.current_value = calc.last_result;
  calc.last_result
}
```

### History Display

```xiom
fn print_history(calc: &Calculator) {
  let mut i = 0;
  while i < calc.history.len() {
    io.println(calc.history.get(i).unwrap());
    i += 1;
  };
}
```

### Memory Operations

- **Store (MS)**: Save current value to memory
- **Recall (MR)**: Load memory into current value
- **Clear (MC)**: Reset memory to 0
- **Add to memory (M+)**: Add current value to memory

### Example Usage

```
calc = 0
ADD 5 → 5
MULTIPLY 3 → 15
STORE → memory = 15
ADD 10 → 25
RECALL → 15
```

